-- title:
--   Drinfeld chart at a supersingular point, with equivariance riders
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a nonzero $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. Let $L$ be a characteristic-zero field that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{q\ell\}$, let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity and $\xi \in L$ a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity with $\zeta = \xi^{\ell}$. Let $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ be the intersection of the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$ with the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$, and let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((t))$ obtained by adjoining to $L$ the coefficientwise image of the $\mathbb{Q}$-rational $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A \to L$, with uniformiser $\varpi$, and with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A \to L \to K$. Let $j \in K$ be the element whose Laurent expansion is the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the modular $j$-function, $j \neq 0$. Write $X$ for [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout gluing $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $A$-algebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$ to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the algebra of elements integral over $A[j^{-1}]$. Let $z$ be a point of $X$ such that the germ at $z$ of the global section coming from $\varpi$ along $X \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$, and let $y$ be a point of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the finite chart algebra mapping to $z$, supersingular in the sense that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the finite chart algebra with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of elements $j_0$ such that every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $j_0$ has no nonzero $q$-torsion point. The assertion is the existence of: a complete discrete valuation domain $W$ (adically complete for its maximal ideal), a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with $\mathfrak{m}_W = (\sigma\varpi)$; power series $f, u, v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u, v$ units and $f \equiv X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$; and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the $\mathfrak{m}$-adic completion of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ onto $S := W[[X_0,X_1]]/(\sigma\varpi \cdot v - f \cdot u)$, subject to three clauses, stated with $\mathrm{toC} : \mathcal{O}_{X,z} \to \widehat{\mathcal{O}_{X,z}}$ the completion map, $\mathrm{mkS}$ the quotient map onto $S$, and $\mathrm{germY}$ the map taking an element of the finite chart algebra to its germ at $z$ through the identification of that algebra with the sections of the finite chart and the open immersion into $X$. First, $e$ matches constants: for every $a \in A$, the image under $e$ of the completed germ of $a$ is the class of the constant $\sigma a$. Second, equivariance with riders: for every $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ lying in $\Gamma_0(M')$ and every $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ satisfying `IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q^2*M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ` (the predicate comparing, under any embedding $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ sending $\zeta$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$, the $q$-expansion of $\tau x$ with the slash action of `conjElemN q γ⁻¹` on quotients of modular forms for $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions), assuming $\tau$ maps the finite chart algebra into itself and that the induced endomorphism fixes $y$ in the sense that $\tau a - a \in y$ for all chart elements $a$, there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c \in W$ and a matrix $M \in M_2(W)$ with: $\theta \circ e \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY} = e \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY} \circ \tau$ on the chart algebra; $\theta$ fixes all constants $C(w)$, $w \in W$; $\theta(X_{j}) \equiv \sum_i C(M_{ij})X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0, X_1$; $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$, and $M_{ij} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$, modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$; $c \equiv 1 \pmod{\mathfrak{m}_W}$ whenever $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod{\ell}$; and $c \not\equiv 1 \pmod{\mathfrak{m}_W}$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity on $K$. Third, branch identification: for every prime ideal $P$ of $S$ containing the class of $\sigma\varpi$ but not containing both classes of $X_0$ and $X_1$, and containing some element whose linear part is $X_0$ (that is, $X_0$ plus a member of $(X_0,X_1)^2$), an element $a$ of the finite chart algebra has $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(a))$ in the preimage of $P$ under $e$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ in $L((t))$ lies in the image of the maximal ideal of $A$ under $A \to L$.
--
--   This is the local structure theorem of Drinfeld and Katz–Mazur at a supersingular point of the fibre over $q$: the completed local ring of the integral model is $W[[X_0,X_1]]/(\varpi v - fu)$ with $f$ congruent to the Drinfeld form $X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ to order $q+2$, the level automorphisms act with linear part a scalar multiple of $\gamma$, and the cusp branch is cut out by the vanishing of all Laurent coefficients modulo the maximal ideal. Here it is given in the $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ frame with constants $\mathbb{Q}(\xi)$, with no lower bound imposed on $q$; two downstream results open this existential and repackage it.
